---
import PhotoSlot from './PhotoSlot.astro';
import MehndiMotif from './ornaments/MehndiMotif.astro';
---

<section id="about" class="section">
  <div class="shell grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-20">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow text-forest">The Artist</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 text-4xl text-espresso md:text-5xl">Artistry Rooted in Tradition</h2>
      <MehndiMotif class="my-7 w-40 text-beige" />

      <div class="lede space-y-5 text-espresso">
        <p>
          I learned mehndi the way most of us learn anything that matters — sitting close to
          someone who had been doing it for thirty years, asking what each part meant before
          asking how to draw it.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every design begins with a conversation. What you are carrying that day, who matters
          most in the room, what your mother or grandmother would recognise in it. The patterns
          are traditional because the tradition earns it, not because it is a trend.
        </p>
        <p>
          I work slowly and I only take a limited number of weddings each season, so nothing I
          draw is rushed. That is the whole promise: unhurried work, made for one occasion.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a href="#contact" class="btn btn-ghost mt-9">Meet the Artist</a>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <PhotoSlot
        alt="Portrait of Hamna, a mehndi artist at work in her studio"
        label="Your portrait here"
        class="aspect-[4/5] w-full"
      />
      <p class="mt-4 text-center text-sm text-espresso">
        Replace with a portrait of Hamna
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
